-- **`applyChange`**: Behind the scenes, the helper methods call `applyChange`, which triggers a global state update and UI refresh. Stateful helpers accept an optional stable, untranslated `parameterKey`; use it for new or actively maintained controls so Undo merging and Reset/default metadata do not depend on the visible label. Keys identify the complete processing role, not just the caption: controls in different stages that intentionally share text (for example the Screen panel's pre- and post-demosaic `Strength` controls) must have different keys. The Screen panel provides a complete example under `screen.*`, Geometry follows under `geometry.*`, and Image Layer uses `image_layer.*`. Do not assign keys to panel-local operation/presentation toggles merely because they use a `ParameterPanel` helper; Geometry's Auto fit/nonlinear-request toggles and Image Layer's Set-by-area/channel buttons are intentionally unkeyed because they are not saved `ParameterState`. Keyed numeric helpers can opt into the standard default presentation: the label becomes semibold and a small Reset control appears only while the value differs from a fresh `ParameterState` default. Reset remains a separate undo gesture. Preserve explicit sentinel values such as `0 = not configured/process default`: when a sentinel lies below the ordinary numeric interval, pass it as the helper's separate special minimum instead of clamping it to the first explicit value. Screen geometry follows the same rule: fresh `scr_to_img_parameters` have zero coordinate vectors, meaning geometry has not been established. `screen_has_regular_geometry_p(type)` says only that the selected process has a regular lattice; code that consumes screen/final coordinates must use `screen_geometry_configured_p(params)` (and still handle `scr_to_img::set_parameters()` failure). Detection/discovery code is the intentional exception because it establishes the mapping.
